\subtree[tot-565J]{
  \author{emilyriehl}
  \title{Full subcategories}
  \meta{source}{[PR\startverb#\stopverb213](https://github.com/samtoth/agda-synthetic-categories/pull/213)}

  \p{[Emily](emilyriehl) formalised the construction of [full subtypes](stt-00U5)
    using the [sharp modality](stt-00JF). Given a family of propositions
  #{\phi : \flat A \to \Prop}, we construct a type #{A_{\phi}} with an inclusion into
  #{A}, the [universal property](stt-00U8) for full subtypes says that this map is orthogonal
  to every #{\flat} counit. Under the assumption that the global points of the interval
  are just the two endpoints (i.e that the canonical inclusion #{\partial \Delta^1 \to \Delta^1}
  is equivalent to the #{\flat} counit of #{\Delta^1}), it follows that this inclusion
  is a [fully-faithful](stt-00LR) map.}

  \p{It has been left for future work to show that when #{A} is a category, then so is
  #{A_{\phi}}.}

  \subtree{
  \title{New modules}

  \ul{
  \li{\ref{Synthetic.Categories.FullSubcategories}}
  }
  }
}

\subtree{
  \title{Reflections}

  \p{One of the most obvious places where the library needed improvement was
     in the documentation:
  \ul{
    \li{There is no (easily accessible) 'index' page where you can view
    all the modules. (We have since added a link to the Everything.agda on the homepage,
    but there's probably still opportunity to improve here)}
    \li{The search feature doesn't work too well at the moment. Currently
         Forester doesn't support full text search as far as I know; however it
    might be possible to hack something together with a custom theme.
    It would also be nice to be able to search Agda definitions directly through the
    search on Forester. [[martinescardo]] has recently made a [very nice tool](https://martinescardo.github.io/TypeTopologySearch.html) for
    searching though the [[typeTopology]] library from which we could take some inspiration.}
    \li{Relatedly, there are some links on the rendered Agda 
    which don't take you to the correct tree. This is a bit tricky to fix as the bug stems
 from a mismatch in how Forester and Agda handle unicode.}
}
  }

